1
00:00:19,975 --> 00:00:24,445
(Today's My Star and Seo Jin share a special connection.)

2
00:00:24,875 --> 00:00:28,044
When did you meet him for the first time?

3
00:00:28,045 --> 00:00:29,844
(When did you meet My Star for the first time?)

4
00:00:29,845 --> 00:00:32,914
As far as I can remember, I was in my 20s.

5
00:00:32,915 --> 00:00:33,955
How did you guys meet?

6
00:00:34,655 --> 00:00:36,825
He's friends with everyone around me.

7
00:00:42,195 --> 00:00:44,124
(A basketball legend...)

8
00:00:44,125 --> 00:00:46,565
(who once dominated the court)

9
00:00:47,135 --> 00:00:51,375
(Korea's national treasure of a center, Seo Jang Hoon)

10
00:00:53,905 --> 00:00:57,775
(Seo Jin, who gave off the vibe of a manager who'd studied abroad)

11
00:00:58,775 --> 00:01:01,684
He's around my age, and we grew up in the same era.

12
00:01:01,685 --> 00:01:02,845
(They spent their youth together.)

13
00:01:03,515 --> 00:01:04,955
I thought he was the funniest.

14
00:01:05,955 --> 00:01:08,025
I said, "You're the funniest person I know."

15
00:01:08,055 --> 00:01:10,425
And he was like, "Hey, you're the funniest to me."

16
00:01:11,495 --> 00:01:12,754
I love him.

17
00:01:12,755 --> 00:01:15,025
(My Star has been his beloved friend for 30 years.)

18
00:01:15,125 --> 00:01:17,465
Is there anything about him that you're jealous of?

19
00:01:18,835 --> 00:01:20,334
(Thinking)

20
00:01:20,335 --> 00:01:22,065
- His wealth? - Wealth?

21
00:01:22,265 --> 00:01:23,635
Who is richer?

22
00:01:23,905 --> 00:01:25,275
I'm sure Jang Hoon is richer.

23
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:26,705
Have you even tried comparing?

24
00:01:27,035 --> 00:01:28,704
There's no need. I surrender.

25
00:01:28,705 --> 00:01:29,945
(A fortune so immense that even the Young Master bows out?)

26
00:01:30,075 --> 00:01:32,075
Someone has a lump of gold.

27
00:01:32,145 --> 00:01:33,245
That's Young Master.

28
00:01:33,575 --> 00:01:35,615
Someone has ten lumps of gold.

29
00:01:36,185 --> 00:01:37,414
That's My Lord.

30
00:01:37,415 --> 00:01:39,614
(Lord Seo Jang Hoon)

31
00:01:39,615 --> 00:01:41,785
He's the wealthiest person I've met.

32
00:01:41,825 --> 00:01:43,255
My Lord.

33
00:01:43,785 --> 00:01:45,554
Is it okay to spend over 10,000 dollars on a get-together?

34
00:01:45,555 --> 00:01:46,594
Yes.

35
00:01:46,595 --> 00:01:47,795
You can spend that much money?

36
00:01:47,895 --> 00:01:49,264
With a net worth of two billion dollars,

37
00:01:49,265 --> 00:01:51,864
even if you spend 100,000 dollars a day, you'd never run out of money.

38
00:01:51,865 --> 00:01:53,564
Gosh, that's impossible.

39
00:01:53,565 --> 00:01:54,735
Why did you put the building up for sale?

40
00:01:55,265 --> 00:01:58,575
(Will he manage My Star's assets for the first time on the show?)

41
00:01:58,805 --> 00:02:03,374
(A billionaire giant)

42
00:02:03,375 --> 00:02:06,115
(But there's something he has more of than money.)

43
00:02:06,715 --> 00:02:08,445
Why are you so mad?

44
00:02:08,615 --> 00:02:09,714
It's because I'm mad.

45
00:02:09,715 --> 00:02:11,044
(He has a short temper.)

46
00:02:11,045 --> 00:02:12,114
I've never met anyone...

47
00:02:12,115 --> 00:02:14,824
who complains as much as he does in my entire life.

48
00:02:14,825 --> 00:02:17,355
He used to glare at people.

49
00:02:17,525 --> 00:02:19,494
Foul!

50
00:02:19,495 --> 00:02:21,295
(He shows explosive rage on "Divorce Camp.")

51
00:02:21,325 --> 00:02:22,394
What are you doing?

52
00:02:22,395 --> 00:02:26,534
(A man who's always angry whenever he's on TV)

53
00:02:26,535 --> 00:02:29,804
(An angry giant)

54
00:02:29,805 --> 00:02:34,275
(But there's one person who can match him)

55
00:02:34,905 --> 00:02:36,344
You should teach Jang Hoon.

56
00:02:36,345 --> 00:02:37,974
You didn't study much as a kid because you were playing sports.

57
00:02:37,975 --> 00:02:39,144
He didn't have time to study because he was busy training.

58
00:02:39,145 --> 00:02:40,545
Do you even know how to write your name in Chinese characters?

59
00:02:41,285 --> 00:02:43,244
You've just crossed the line.

60
00:02:43,245 --> 00:02:45,154
"Do you even know how to write your name in Chinese characters?"

61
00:02:45,155 --> 00:02:46,414
(He's laughing so hard he's about to cry.)

62
00:02:46,415 --> 00:02:47,555
That's ridiculous!

63
00:02:48,785 --> 00:02:49,884
(Rage explosion)

64
00:02:49,885 --> 00:02:50,885
It's funny.

65
00:02:50,886 --> 00:02:52,595
I like when Jang Hoon reacts like that.

66
00:02:52,625 --> 00:02:54,255
I love it when he gets mad.

67
00:02:55,325 --> 00:02:57,364
(I'd love to see Seo Jin and Jang Hoon together.)

68
00:02:57,365 --> 00:02:58,665
(They're both Thinkers.)

69
00:02:58,835 --> 00:03:00,695
I'm a Thinker, but have a warm heart.

70
00:03:00,865 --> 00:03:02,535
- Seo Jin is grumpy. - Yes.

71
00:03:03,235 --> 00:03:05,304
(Cold Thinker Young Master...)

72
00:03:05,305 --> 00:03:07,105
(versus Warm Thinker Lord)

73
00:03:07,875 --> 00:03:11,545
(Who will win the Thinker battle between these friends of 30 years?)

74
00:03:12,515 --> 00:03:15,685
(A makeup studio in Cheogdam-dong at 9am)

75
00:03:16,745 --> 00:03:20,415
(He casually gets his makeup done while waiting for the secretaries.)

76
00:03:21,325 --> 00:03:24,055
I might be running late at this rate.

77
00:03:25,055 --> 00:03:27,025
(The secretaries are here.)

78
00:03:27,695 --> 00:03:29,124
- Hello. - Hello.

79
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:30,265
- Hello. - Hello.

80
00:03:30,465 --> 00:03:31,864
- Hello. - Are you the manager?

81
00:03:31,865 --> 00:03:33,835
I'm Ko Hag Yun. And I'm Jang Hoon's manager.

82
00:03:34,495 --> 00:03:36,535
I'm Ko Hag Yun. And I'm Jang Hoon's manager.

83
00:03:37,165 --> 00:03:39,034
- Were you a basketball player too? - No.

84
00:03:39,035 --> 00:03:40,875
- No? - No.

85
00:03:40,935 --> 00:03:42,644
Were you a martial artist?

86
00:03:42,645 --> 00:03:44,245
- No. - You look like an athlete.

87
00:03:44,675 --> 00:03:45,774
- You were an athlete, right? - No.

88
00:03:45,775 --> 00:03:46,945
No?

89
00:03:47,175 --> 00:03:49,285
(I was scared for no reason.)

90
00:03:49,945 --> 00:03:52,784
You know Jang Hoon is very meticulous about hygiene.

91
00:03:52,785 --> 00:03:53,855
- Yes. - So...

92
00:03:54,315 --> 00:03:56,285
- he... - Why are you shaking? Relax.

93
00:03:56,355 --> 00:03:57,625
Don't be nervous.

94
00:03:58,525 --> 00:03:59,955
(Come to think of it...)

95
00:04:00,225 --> 00:04:03,564
(Shaking)

96
00:04:03,565 --> 00:04:04,994
Why are you shaking? Relax.

97
00:04:04,995 --> 00:04:06,865
(Licking)

98
00:04:07,335 --> 00:04:08,935
(He doesn't know where to look.)

99
00:04:09,405 --> 00:04:12,535
Why are you shaking? Relax.

100
00:04:14,205 --> 00:04:15,904
- Does he punch you or something? - No.

101
00:04:15,905 --> 00:04:17,605
Why are you shaking so much?

102
00:04:17,705 --> 00:04:18,815
It's my first time on TV.

103
00:04:20,875 --> 00:04:22,444
(My gosh)

104
00:04:22,445 --> 00:04:24,615
Today, he's going to film...

105
00:04:25,155 --> 00:04:27,354
his EBS show, "Seo Jang Hoon's Millionaire Next Door,"

106
00:04:27,355 --> 00:04:29,984
which he hosts.

107
00:04:29,985 --> 00:04:32,955
(The show he hosts...)

108
00:04:33,795 --> 00:04:36,295
(travels across the country to meet millionaires...)

109
00:04:36,895 --> 00:04:40,495
(and uncovers the secrets to their success.)

110
00:04:40,635 --> 00:04:42,235
(His number one concern is revenue.)

111
00:04:42,405 --> 00:04:43,565
(Daily revenue of 1.2 million dollars)

112
00:04:43,665 --> 00:04:44,935
(Annual revenue up to 48 million dollars)

113
00:04:45,035 --> 00:04:46,535
(Annual revenue of over 100 million dollars)

114
00:04:47,775 --> 00:04:48,775
(Impressed)

115
00:04:49,545 --> 00:04:53,715
(Evey week, he goes in search of people who are truly rich.)

116
00:04:53,775 --> 00:04:56,084
Today, he's going to film his EBS show...

117
00:04:56,085 --> 00:04:57,385
"Seo Jang Hoon's Millionaire Next Door," which he hosts.

118
00:04:57,615 --> 00:04:58,985
The filming location is Gangneung.

119
00:04:59,255 --> 00:05:01,885
(Gangneung?)

120
00:05:02,925 --> 00:05:05,624
(Seoul, Gangneung)

121
00:05:05,625 --> 00:05:08,125
(Today, they have to drive more than 3 hours each way.)

122
00:05:08,195 --> 00:05:11,025
The second shoot will take place...

123
00:05:11,195 --> 00:05:12,834
- I see. - at Haslla Art World,

124
00:05:12,835 --> 00:05:14,495
which is run by a millionaire.

125
00:05:14,935 --> 00:05:17,805
You know Jang Hoon is very meticulous about hygiene.

126
00:05:17,905 --> 00:05:19,675
(I know it very well.)

127
00:05:19,805 --> 00:05:22,345
It's an emergency whenever he needs to find a restroom.

128
00:05:22,775 --> 00:05:25,145
You have to find a clean restroom.

129
00:05:25,875 --> 00:05:28,485
Does he not use the restrooms at highway rest stops?

130
00:05:28,545 --> 00:05:29,985
He doesn't really use them.

131
00:05:30,315 --> 00:05:32,885
Then what kind of restrooms does he use on the highway?

132
00:05:33,255 --> 00:05:34,515
He usually just holds it in.

133
00:05:34,855 --> 00:05:36,185
- He holds it in? - He's that picky?

134
00:05:37,155 --> 00:05:38,794
You know my personality.

135
00:05:38,795 --> 00:05:39,855
- I see. - I see.

136
00:05:40,055 --> 00:05:42,694
(Being a germaphobe,)

137
00:05:42,695 --> 00:05:45,695
(his weakness is public restrooms.)

138
00:05:45,895 --> 00:05:48,004
It's good to drink a lot of water.

139
00:05:48,005 --> 00:05:49,805
He doesn't drink water because he doesn't want to use the restroom.

140
00:05:50,205 --> 00:05:52,405
The restroom here is nice. Do you want to go?

141
00:05:52,535 --> 00:05:54,435
- Maybe later. I'll think about it. - Okay.

142
00:05:54,905 --> 00:05:57,245
(They might have to manager even his bodily functions.)

143
00:05:57,845 --> 00:06:00,514
I'd appreciate it if you could find a clean restroom for him.

144
00:06:00,515 --> 00:06:01,585
(I knew it.)

145
00:06:01,745 --> 00:06:05,584
And he doesn't eat during a shoot.

146
00:06:05,585 --> 00:06:07,585
- Does he eat nothing? All day? - He doesn't eat at all.

147
00:06:08,555 --> 00:06:11,495
It's Jang Hoon.

148
00:06:12,595 --> 00:06:13,794
(Glaring)

149
00:06:13,795 --> 00:06:16,064
- Are they still not here? - They're talking.

150
00:06:16,065 --> 00:06:18,034
(Are they still not here?)

151
00:06:18,035 --> 00:06:20,594
(He's worried about being late for the shoot.)

152
00:06:20,595 --> 00:06:22,165
They shouldn't take this long.

153
00:06:23,035 --> 00:06:26,705
It takes 2 hours and 50 minutes to get there.

154
00:06:28,205 --> 00:06:30,404
(Displeased)

155
00:06:30,405 --> 00:06:32,845
Since he's tall,

156
00:06:32,975 --> 00:06:36,015
be careful not to let his head get caught on the branches.

157
00:06:36,115 --> 00:06:37,985
We can't even see them.

158
00:06:38,385 --> 00:06:39,985
I always keep an eye on it.

159
00:06:40,555 --> 00:06:43,154
(This is quite unusual.)

160
00:06:43,155 --> 00:06:46,024
When he's feeling down,

161
00:06:46,025 --> 00:06:48,465
show him cute videos or photos of puppies or babies.

162
00:06:48,565 --> 00:06:49,665
Does he have a dog?

163
00:06:50,325 --> 00:06:51,835
- You... - Babies?

164
00:06:52,535 --> 00:06:54,465
- Does he like babies? - Yes.

165
00:06:54,595 --> 00:06:55,705
- And... - He's crazy.

166
00:06:56,305 --> 00:06:58,105
(Gasping)

167
00:06:58,835 --> 00:07:01,505
(Is someone talking about me behind my back?)

168
00:07:02,045 --> 00:07:05,044
I took a video of a baby a few days ago.

169
00:07:05,045 --> 00:07:07,215
- You did? - I can show it to him.

170
00:07:07,475 --> 00:07:09,115
I was at a housewarming party.

171
00:07:10,115 --> 00:07:11,685
- What's this? - The bag you need on set.

172
00:07:12,415 --> 00:07:14,584
Why are there so many things?

173
00:07:14,585 --> 00:07:15,655
(A bag full of items for Giant)

174
00:07:16,625 --> 00:07:18,695
(Heavy)

175
00:07:19,155 --> 00:07:20,355
Why are there so many things?

176
00:07:21,495 --> 00:07:23,425
(The bag is full of something.)

177
00:07:24,725 --> 00:07:25,964
It's hand wash.

178
00:07:25,965 --> 00:07:28,265
(Everyone pauses.)

179
00:07:28,705 --> 00:07:31,005
(As expected, there's a hygiene item.)

180
00:07:31,505 --> 00:07:33,935
(You can already guess what the rest of the items are.)

181
00:07:34,435 --> 00:07:37,275
(They're finally going to meet My Star.)

182
00:07:38,545 --> 00:07:39,545
Jang Hoon.

183
00:07:41,275 --> 00:07:42,944
- Hello. - We might be running late.

184
00:07:42,945 --> 00:07:43,945
There was so much traffic.

185
00:07:43,946 --> 00:07:45,684
(These best friends haven't met for a while.)

186
00:07:45,685 --> 00:07:46,984
- Hello. - Oh, my.

187
00:07:46,985 --> 00:07:48,585
- It's cold. Take this. - What's this?

188
00:07:49,025 --> 00:07:51,425
- This is what you're advertising. - Yes.

189
00:07:52,495 --> 00:07:54,694
I was actually going to buy one.

190
00:07:54,695 --> 00:07:56,795
Use these blankets to sit on or cover yourself with.

191
00:07:56,965 --> 00:07:58,025
Thank you.

192
00:07:58,135 --> 00:08:00,394
I see this brand's store every day...

193
00:08:00,395 --> 00:08:01,765
on my commute,

194
00:08:02,335 --> 00:08:05,905
so I thought I should buy one.

195
00:08:05,975 --> 00:08:07,234
You can just tell me.

196
00:08:07,235 --> 00:08:08,944
Thank you.

197
00:08:08,945 --> 00:08:10,704
You can wash it with water,

198
00:08:10,705 --> 00:08:12,515
so you can just throw it in the wash whenever you want.

199
00:08:13,475 --> 00:08:14,674
You can wash it often.

200
00:08:14,675 --> 00:08:16,445
I'm sure you'll wash it every day.

201
00:08:16,545 --> 00:08:18,785
I wash my blankets every day, so this is nice.

202
00:08:18,855 --> 00:08:20,555
Thank you.

203
00:08:20,885 --> 00:08:22,925
Apparently, wool is good for men.

204
00:08:24,085 --> 00:08:28,495
(My Star is happy with the gift.)

205
00:08:29,095 --> 00:08:31,394
We have a long drive ahead of us, and you guys came.

206
00:08:31,395 --> 00:08:33,895
- Of all days. - Right. Of all days.

207
00:08:34,465 --> 00:08:36,365
Are you okay with driving?

208
00:08:36,805 --> 00:08:39,035
Gangneung is far.

209
00:08:39,235 --> 00:08:40,334
And it's raining too.

210
00:08:40,335 --> 00:08:42,244
(The estimated driving time is 3 and a half hours.)

211
00:08:42,245 --> 00:08:43,945
(And it's raining.)

212
00:08:44,205 --> 00:08:45,644
- I know. - He won't say a thing...

213
00:08:45,645 --> 00:08:47,115
while driving.

214
00:08:47,745 --> 00:08:49,485
I feel nervous too.

215
00:08:51,555 --> 00:08:53,214
His eyesight has gotten a lot worse lately.

216
00:08:53,215 --> 00:08:55,124
(Aged eyes on top of wet roads)

217
00:08:55,125 --> 00:08:58,024
You have trouble seeing small things and things up close.

218
00:08:58,025 --> 00:09:00,324
(Spraying)

219
00:09:00,325 --> 00:09:02,865
I have trouble seeing my phone screen.

220
00:09:03,565 --> 00:09:05,664
(Looking intently)

221
00:09:05,665 --> 00:09:09,005
Gosh. She's using a lot of hairspray.

222
00:09:09,365 --> 00:09:10,734
- Are you jealous? - What?

223
00:09:10,735 --> 00:09:12,905
- Are you jealous? - I am.

224
00:09:13,305 --> 00:09:14,334
(My Star has hair that needs to be kept in place.)

225
00:09:14,335 --> 00:09:16,745
- You should use some too. - No, I can't.

226
00:09:17,875 --> 00:09:19,174
His hair doesn't look like it's going anywhere.

227
00:09:19,175 --> 00:09:20,774
(Confirmed by a hair expert)

228
00:09:20,775 --> 00:09:22,215
He has thick hair.

229
00:09:23,015 --> 00:09:25,014
She used half a can of hairspray.

230
00:09:25,015 --> 00:09:27,355
(Even after using half a can of hairspray,)

231
00:09:28,185 --> 00:09:30,225
(his thick hair stays perfectly slicked back,)

232
00:09:30,825 --> 00:09:33,095
(even in rain or snow.)

233
00:09:33,495 --> 00:09:34,994
His hair is really thick.

234
00:09:34,995 --> 00:09:36,965
(This is his signature hairstyle.)

235
00:09:37,725 --> 00:09:40,935
She's been styling my hair...

236
00:09:41,235 --> 00:09:42,665
this way...

237
00:09:43,365 --> 00:09:45,475
for about 12 years.

238
00:09:46,775 --> 00:09:48,804
She's the best in the country at this hairstyle.

239
00:09:48,805 --> 00:09:49,974
(The ultimate slicked-back hair expert)

240
00:09:49,975 --> 00:09:51,275
Because she does it...

241
00:09:51,675 --> 00:09:53,545
every day.

242
00:09:54,745 --> 00:09:56,185
I need...

243
00:09:57,115 --> 00:10:00,585
to come here every day.

244
00:10:00,655 --> 00:10:02,685
I can't get it done on set.

245
00:10:02,785 --> 00:10:04,425
No one else can style my hair like this.

246
00:10:06,195 --> 00:10:07,854
- It's neat. - My gosh.

247
00:10:07,855 --> 00:10:09,664
You look sleek and neat.

248
00:10:09,665 --> 00:10:11,424
- Let's go. - How about your clothes?

249
00:10:11,425 --> 00:10:12,964
- I should get changed. - Here?

250
00:10:12,965 --> 00:10:14,165
No.

251
00:10:15,005 --> 00:10:16,965
- Thank you. Have a nice day. - Thank you.

252
00:10:19,235 --> 00:10:21,805
- Jang Hoon, get in the car quickly. - Yes.

253
00:10:22,975 --> 00:10:25,674
- Oh, my. - Please open the back door.

254
00:10:25,675 --> 00:10:26,715
Sure.

255
00:10:27,115 --> 00:10:28,815
- Welcome. - Oh, my.

256
00:10:29,585 --> 00:10:32,085
My goodness.

257
00:10:32,955 --> 00:10:35,755
Even when I sit in this car,

258
00:10:36,325 --> 00:10:38,655
there's still plenty of room here.

259
00:10:39,425 --> 00:10:41,295
- Isn't it cramped? - No, it's not.

260
00:10:41,725 --> 00:10:43,065
It's a nice car.

261
00:10:43,165 --> 00:10:44,795
The leather looks really nice too.

262
00:10:45,595 --> 00:10:46,965
- Please close the door. - Okay.

263
00:10:47,665 --> 00:10:50,565
(As always, he looks after My Star in his own nonchalant way.)

264
00:10:51,505 --> 00:10:53,405
The window closes in such a cool way.

265
00:10:54,475 --> 00:10:57,775
Try lowering the sunshade.

266
00:10:58,105 --> 00:10:59,914
It'll come down from the top.

267
00:10:59,915 --> 00:11:01,114
Lower it.

268
00:11:01,115 --> 00:11:02,384
(He'll protect My Star's skin.)

269
00:11:02,385 --> 00:11:03,385
And...

270
00:11:04,245 --> 00:11:05,985
this seat has a massage function.

271
00:11:06,115 --> 00:11:07,254
You can control everything with the remote.

272
00:11:07,255 --> 00:11:08,385
That's nice.

273
00:11:08,725 --> 00:11:09,784
(Turning on the massage function)

274
00:11:09,785 --> 00:11:11,184
- Does it work? - Yes, it does.

275
00:11:11,185 --> 00:11:12,695
(Smiling)

276
00:11:12,855 --> 00:11:14,455
Let's get going.

277
00:11:14,625 --> 00:11:16,565
Let me know if you need anything.

278
00:11:16,895 --> 00:11:18,534
Thank you.

279
00:11:18,535 --> 00:11:19,835
(To the studio in Gangneung for his first scheduled shoot)

280
00:11:20,665 --> 00:11:22,234
It's an honor...

281
00:11:22,235 --> 00:11:24,664
to ride in a car driven by Kwang Kyu.

282
00:11:24,665 --> 00:11:26,904
- No, it's an honor for me... - No.

283
00:11:26,905 --> 00:11:29,344
to drive for a billionaire like you.

284
00:11:29,345 --> 00:11:30,405
"A billionaire?"

285
00:11:30,545 --> 00:11:34,745
You're like My Lord.

286
00:11:34,945 --> 00:11:37,785
(My Lord)

287
00:11:38,185 --> 00:11:42,284
Have you eaten, My Star? Did you have breakfast?

288
00:11:42,285 --> 00:11:44,855
I don't eat anything.

289
00:11:45,195 --> 00:11:46,995
- Not before a shoot? - No.

290
00:11:47,795 --> 00:11:49,125
When do you eat then?

291
00:11:49,295 --> 00:11:50,995
I eat at home after everything is over.

292
00:11:51,765 --> 00:11:54,435
- So do you eat once a day? - Yes.

293
00:11:55,805 --> 00:11:57,235
You must be hungry.

294
00:11:57,465 --> 00:12:01,674
I do a lot of shoots where I watch videos.

295
00:12:01,675 --> 00:12:03,344
Right. Most of the time.

296
00:12:03,345 --> 00:12:06,215
When I keep watching videos,

297
00:12:07,275 --> 00:12:09,114
I get sleepy.

298
00:12:09,115 --> 00:12:12,085
And I have to use the restroom.

299
00:12:12,415 --> 00:12:15,625
You work so hard even if you have a lot of money.

300
00:12:16,725 --> 00:12:18,794
Your net worth is in the hundreds of millions of dollars.

301
00:12:18,795 --> 00:12:20,124
My net worth is what?

302
00:12:20,125 --> 00:12:21,324
Hundreds of millions of dollars.

303
00:12:21,325 --> 00:12:23,965
No, I don't have that much money.

304
00:12:24,365 --> 00:12:26,535
By the way, why did you put the building up for sale?

305
00:12:27,435 --> 00:12:29,604
There were articles about it.

306
00:12:29,605 --> 00:12:31,065
- The building? - I want to buy it.

307
00:12:31,835 --> 00:12:33,635
So how many buildings do you have?

308
00:12:33,875 --> 00:12:35,645
- Sorry? - How many buildings do you have?

309
00:12:35,875 --> 00:12:38,045
Two or three?

310
00:12:38,675 --> 00:12:40,515
(He has 3 buildings.)

311
00:12:40,715 --> 00:12:42,444
- I have three. - You do?

312
00:12:42,445 --> 00:12:45,215
I want to buy it.

313
00:12:45,955 --> 00:12:47,014
Go ahead.

314
00:12:47,015 --> 00:12:48,155
You don't have money.

315
00:12:48,655 --> 00:12:50,985
Everyone has their own struggles.

316
00:12:53,325 --> 00:12:54,425
My gosh.

317
00:12:54,795 --> 00:12:57,495
Hee Chul kept saying...

318
00:12:57,595 --> 00:13:00,165
on "Men on a Mission..."

319
00:13:00,695 --> 00:13:02,864
that I had hundreds of millions of dollars,

320
00:13:02,865 --> 00:13:04,064
and eventually, he even claimed I had two billion dollars.

321
00:13:04,065 --> 00:13:05,505
Right. Over a billion dollars.

322
00:13:06,305 --> 00:13:09,875
So everyone thinks I have two billion dollars.

323
00:13:10,075 --> 00:13:12,344
But do you know how many people in our country...

324
00:13:12,345 --> 00:13:13,675
have a net worth of over two billion dollars?

325
00:13:14,175 --> 00:13:16,784
Maybe 20 to 30 people?

326
00:13:16,785 --> 00:13:20,214
I looked it up on the Internet.

327
00:13:20,215 --> 00:13:21,215
Okay.

328
00:13:21,355 --> 00:13:22,984
There are 35 people.

329
00:13:22,985 --> 00:13:24,455
And you're one of them?

330
00:13:25,825 --> 00:13:29,165
(Is he 1 of the 35 people?)

331
00:13:29,665 --> 00:13:31,495
You're amazing.

332
00:13:32,095 --> 00:13:34,635
- That means... - My Lord.

333
00:13:35,265 --> 00:13:38,505
five or six out of a hundred people believe it.

334
00:13:39,475 --> 00:13:40,674
They really believe it.

335
00:13:40,675 --> 00:13:41,845
- Right. - I mean...

336
00:13:41,905 --> 00:13:44,004
what could I possibly do...

337
00:13:44,005 --> 00:13:45,214
(I'm not on the list of people worth 2 billion dollars.)

338
00:13:45,215 --> 00:13:49,585
to make two billion dollars? That's what I ask.

339
00:13:50,615 --> 00:13:52,214
How many people do you think in our country...

340
00:13:52,215 --> 00:13:55,685
have a net worth of over 50 million dollars?

341
00:13:55,985 --> 00:13:57,154
- Over 50 million dollars? - Yes.

342
00:13:57,155 --> 00:13:58,754
About 500 people?

343
00:13:58,755 --> 00:14:00,894
- There are about 5,000 people. - About 5,000 people?

344
00:14:00,895 --> 00:14:03,164
- Yes. - And My Lord is one of them.

345
00:14:03,165 --> 00:14:04,465
- Come on. - He is.

346
00:14:05,165 --> 00:14:08,464
(Does he have a net worth of over 50 million dollars?)

347
00:14:08,465 --> 00:14:10,234
- You're not one of them, Seo Jin. - No, I'm not.

348
00:14:10,235 --> 00:14:11,264
Not even close.

349
00:14:11,265 --> 00:14:13,104
- Unfortunately, - It's unfortunate.

350
00:14:13,105 --> 00:14:14,105
Seo Jin...

351
00:14:14,106 --> 00:14:15,475
- doesn't have 50 million dollars. - Not even close.

352
00:14:16,505 --> 00:14:17,844
You must have over five million dollars, though.

353
00:14:17,845 --> 00:14:18,845
But...

354
00:14:18,846 --> 00:14:20,214
With a net worth of two billion dollars,

355
00:14:20,215 --> 00:14:22,744
even if you spend 100,000 dollars a day, you'd never run out of money.

356
00:14:22,745 --> 00:14:24,184
Right. He'll never run out.

357
00:14:24,185 --> 00:14:25,584
- Did you say 100,000 dollars? - Yes.

358
00:14:25,585 --> 00:14:27,115
- That's impossible. - Yes.

359
00:14:27,715 --> 00:14:31,424
Apparently, it's hard to spend ten million dollars a year...

360
00:14:31,425 --> 00:14:33,494
just on everyday living expenses, like food, shopping and drinks.

361
00:14:33,495 --> 00:14:34,825
- It's impossible. - Right.

362
00:14:35,595 --> 00:14:38,165
Even if you have a lot of money,

363
00:14:38,695 --> 00:14:41,834
you wouldn't go to a fancy sushi restaurant every day.

364
00:14:41,835 --> 00:14:43,005
- No, you wouldn't. - Right?

365
00:14:43,235 --> 00:14:47,274
I want to eat gimbap and doenjang stew too.

366
00:14:47,275 --> 00:14:49,474
Even if it's expensive...

367
00:14:49,475 --> 00:14:50,475
(Even if you spend a lot, it's hard to spend 10 million dollars a year.)

368
00:14:50,476 --> 00:14:52,575
- Even if you try hard... - Even if you buy expensive stuff...

369
00:14:53,145 --> 00:14:54,374
It's not easy...

370
00:14:54,375 --> 00:14:57,115
- to go shopping every day... - Or to buy luxury goods.

371
00:14:57,645 --> 00:14:59,785
You could just buy your girlfriend a bag every day.

372
00:15:00,085 --> 00:15:01,784
Still, it's not easy to do it...

373
00:15:01,785 --> 00:15:03,384
- every day. - How can you go shopping every day?

374
00:15:03,385 --> 00:15:05,125
How can you go to a department store every day?

375
00:15:07,625 --> 00:15:09,424
I wish I had ten million dollars.

376
00:15:09,425 --> 00:15:11,164
(The driver can't relate to it.)

377
00:15:11,165 --> 00:15:14,895
How did you become so rich?

378
00:15:14,965 --> 00:15:16,035
Gosh.

379
00:15:17,165 --> 00:15:19,535
- How? - I'm not that rich.

380
00:15:19,935 --> 00:15:22,075
I didn't spend the money I made...

381
00:15:23,275 --> 00:15:24,975
as an athlete,

382
00:15:25,615 --> 00:15:27,245
so I was able...

383
00:15:28,145 --> 00:15:30,215
to keep saving it.

384
00:15:31,045 --> 00:15:34,514
I saved the money I earned,

385
00:15:34,515 --> 00:15:36,485
and over time,

386
00:15:37,255 --> 00:15:39,325
it just kept growing.

387
00:15:40,155 --> 00:15:42,965
- I think this is the key. - It's very important.

388
00:15:43,625 --> 00:15:47,034
What do you spend most of your money on these days?

389
00:15:47,035 --> 00:15:48,394
- Me? - I'm curious. Yes.

390
00:15:48,395 --> 00:15:50,435
The only thing...

391
00:15:50,805 --> 00:15:53,605
I spend money on for myself each month is...

392
00:15:54,335 --> 00:15:56,145
(Does he buy a building?)

393
00:15:56,605 --> 00:15:58,375
(Does he invest in stocks?)

394
00:15:58,545 --> 00:16:01,375
food delivery.

395
00:16:02,145 --> 00:16:03,544
That's the only thing.

396
00:16:03,545 --> 00:16:05,554
(For a man worth 2 billion dollars, he lives a rather modest lifestyle.)

397
00:16:05,555 --> 00:16:07,184
I don't buy anything.

398
00:16:07,185 --> 00:16:08,954
I want to buy clothes,

399
00:16:08,955 --> 00:16:10,855
but nothing fits.

400
00:16:11,455 --> 00:16:14,624
(He saves money on everything except food.)

401
00:16:14,625 --> 00:16:17,695
Do you try to save electricity at home too?

402
00:16:18,325 --> 00:16:20,065
- I do. - You do?

403
00:16:20,265 --> 00:16:22,234
Seo Jin is no joke.

404
00:16:22,235 --> 00:16:24,405
I also save a lot.

405
00:16:24,435 --> 00:16:26,574
I try to keep my expenses...

406
00:16:26,575 --> 00:16:28,745
as low as possible.

407
00:16:29,005 --> 00:16:30,475
That's the right thing.

408
00:16:31,175 --> 00:16:32,975
That's a good habit.

409
00:16:33,345 --> 00:16:36,615
I'm in good hands with two billionaires.

410
00:16:36,815 --> 00:16:37,844
Oh, my.

411
00:16:37,845 --> 00:16:39,384
Jang Hoon...

412
00:16:39,385 --> 00:16:43,355
once treated me, Yu Hui Yeol, and Na Yeong Seok...

413
00:16:43,685 --> 00:16:44,955
to a really nice meal.

414
00:16:45,995 --> 00:16:47,094
(When My Star treats people, he goes all out.)

415
00:16:47,095 --> 00:16:48,424
He treated us to a really nice meal.

416
00:16:48,425 --> 00:16:50,465
Yeong Seok went to the same college as Jang Hoon.

417
00:16:51,495 --> 00:16:55,034
- Oh, right. - He's two years younger than me,

418
00:16:55,035 --> 00:16:57,965
and he was a year behind me in college.

419
00:16:58,635 --> 00:17:01,474
He probably didn't even dare look at you back then.

420
00:17:01,475 --> 00:17:02,904
- I didn't know him back then. - It was impossible.

421
00:17:02,905 --> 00:17:07,514
He was a superstar at Yonsei University.

422
00:17:07,515 --> 00:17:08,844
(He was a star basketball player at Yonsei University.)

423
00:17:08,845 --> 00:17:11,884
- Right. - Back then, his basketball team...

424
00:17:11,885 --> 00:17:13,085
was legendary.

425
00:17:14,215 --> 00:17:18,085
(My Star, Jang Hoon, was a legend.)

426
00:17:18,925 --> 00:17:20,354
(The youngest-ever MVP...)

427
00:17:20,355 --> 00:17:21,825
(of the Korean Basketball Festival in 1993 and 1994)

428
00:17:22,595 --> 00:17:25,995
(League leader in rebounds in his rookie season in 1998)

429
00:17:26,295 --> 00:17:27,864
(A 2-time regular-season MVP)

430
00:17:27,865 --> 00:17:29,965
(A 2-time championship winner)

431
00:17:30,105 --> 00:17:34,334
(My Star was basketball itself.)

432
00:17:34,335 --> 00:17:35,874
There was a rumor...

433
00:17:35,875 --> 00:17:37,375
that whenever the Yonsei University basketball team...

434
00:17:37,975 --> 00:17:39,874
went to a local bar,

435
00:17:39,875 --> 00:17:42,245
they'd start off by drinking 40,000ml of beer per person.

436
00:17:43,545 --> 00:17:44,585
Who does that?

437
00:17:45,485 --> 00:17:46,585
Who does that?

438
00:17:47,655 --> 00:17:49,084
It must be 4L.

439
00:17:49,085 --> 00:17:51,125
No, I heard they drank 40L of beer.

440
00:17:51,385 --> 00:17:55,625
The most beer I've ever seen anyone drink...

441
00:17:56,925 --> 00:17:58,525
was 20 to 30L.

442
00:17:59,565 --> 00:18:01,494
- That's a lot. - It's impossible. That's a lot.

443
00:18:01,495 --> 00:18:02,935
- That's a lot of beer. - So...

444
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:04,834
Do you drink about 10L of beer?

445
00:18:04,835 --> 00:18:06,234
No.

446
00:18:06,235 --> 00:18:07,634
- Not anymore. - He can handle it.

447
00:18:07,635 --> 00:18:08,875
I'm too old now.

448
00:18:08,945 --> 00:18:11,744
Have you ever finished a whole bottle of liquor then?

449
00:18:11,745 --> 00:18:15,144
A bottle? He drinks 2 to 3 bottles.

450
00:18:15,145 --> 00:18:18,314
- He can drink 4 to 5L of liquor. - No.

451
00:18:18,315 --> 00:18:20,684
(Jang Hoon can drink about 6 bottles of liquor.)

452
00:18:20,685 --> 00:18:21,755
No.

453
00:18:21,955 --> 00:18:24,024
No way. 4 to 5L of liquor?

454
00:18:24,025 --> 00:18:25,155
He'll die.

455
00:18:25,355 --> 00:18:28,354
- Liquor? - I used to drink with him a lot.

456
00:18:28,355 --> 00:18:30,624
If you drink 4 to 5L of liquor, you'll die.

457
00:18:30,625 --> 00:18:32,734
No. I'm sure you used to drink that much.

458
00:18:32,735 --> 00:18:34,065
(- You'll die. - No, I saw you drinking that much.)

459
00:18:34,135 --> 00:18:35,765
Alcohol?

460
00:18:36,765 --> 00:18:38,774
I drank with him ten years ago.

461
00:18:38,775 --> 00:18:40,075
There were other people too.

462
00:18:41,475 --> 00:18:42,545
He drank three bottles.

463
00:18:43,245 --> 00:18:44,345
Three bottles of liquor.

464
00:18:46,645 --> 00:18:48,515
(He gets dizzy just by thinking about it.)

465
00:18:48,545 --> 00:18:50,214
I suddenly blacked out.

466
00:18:50,215 --> 00:18:51,584
- Really? - I don't remember anything.

467
00:18:51,585 --> 00:18:53,354
I don't remember what happened after that.

468
00:18:53,355 --> 00:18:54,484
(Even Seo Jin, who can usually hold his liquor, blacked out that day.)

469
00:18:54,485 --> 00:18:56,085
So Jang Hoon can drink more than you.

470
00:18:57,055 --> 00:18:59,255
Isn't it obvious?

471
00:18:59,695 --> 00:19:01,655
Do you think I'd want to outdrink him?

472
00:19:03,395 --> 00:19:06,565
(Jang Hoon is way ahead of him in both money and drinking.)

473
00:19:06,635 --> 00:19:10,034
Has anyone ever asked you to commentate on a basketball game?

474
00:19:10,035 --> 00:19:11,605
- They have. - Okay.

475
00:19:12,005 --> 00:19:14,734
SBS recently asked me to do commentary...

476
00:19:14,735 --> 00:19:17,104
- for the international games. - For Asia?

477
00:19:17,105 --> 00:19:18,675
But I couldn't make it.

478
00:19:18,875 --> 00:19:20,445
- Right. You're doing so many shows. - Yes.

479
00:19:20,675 --> 00:19:22,944
And this is...

480
00:19:22,945 --> 00:19:25,045
what I think.

481
00:19:25,755 --> 00:19:28,185
Basketball isn't my profession anymore.

482
00:19:29,055 --> 00:19:32,695
I don't want to offend the younger players...

483
00:19:33,155 --> 00:19:35,965
or those who are still working in the sport.

484
00:19:36,525 --> 00:19:39,165
So I try to stay away...

485
00:19:39,635 --> 00:19:41,235
from basketball-related interviews and stuff.

486
00:19:41,995 --> 00:19:43,704
You're smart indeed.

487
00:19:43,705 --> 00:19:45,975
(My Star is wise.)

488
00:19:46,775 --> 00:19:49,304
But since you have a connection to international games in Asia,

489
00:19:49,305 --> 00:19:52,345
- Right. - I can see why they'd ask you.

490
00:19:53,115 --> 00:19:55,915
Korea won the gold medal...

491
00:19:56,485 --> 00:19:57,615
at the international event in Busan in 2002,

492
00:19:58,245 --> 00:20:00,485
for the first time...

493
00:20:00,685 --> 00:20:04,025
- in 20 years. - Right.

494
00:20:05,225 --> 00:20:06,695
In 2002,

495
00:20:07,455 --> 00:20:09,025
the Chinese team had Yao Ming.

496
00:20:12,795 --> 00:20:14,535
When he was standing...

497
00:20:14,765 --> 00:20:16,505
in front of me, I couldn't even see the rim.

498
00:20:18,135 --> 00:20:20,575
He's 227cm tall.

499
00:20:20,875 --> 00:20:22,005
He's tall.

500
00:20:22,775 --> 00:20:25,745
(Yao Ming was an NBA superstar at the time.)

501
00:20:26,315 --> 00:20:27,914
Every play starts with Yao Ming.

502
00:20:27,915 --> 00:20:29,715
(He could dunk with just a little jump.)

503
00:20:30,085 --> 00:20:32,314
(He was known as the "Walking Great Wall.")

504
00:20:32,315 --> 00:20:34,654
He was tall even in the NBA.

505
00:20:34,655 --> 00:20:36,685
- He was one of the tallest players. - He was one of the tallest players.

506
00:20:37,685 --> 00:20:40,355
When he waved...

507
00:20:40,955 --> 00:20:42,895
his arms around,

508
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:45,165
I couldn't even see the backboard.

509
00:20:46,435 --> 00:20:47,464
Yao Ming was that tall?

510
00:20:47,465 --> 00:20:48,965
You're lying.

511
00:20:49,565 --> 00:20:51,404
- That's impossible. - Think about it.

512
00:20:51,405 --> 00:20:52,405
You couldn't see the backboard?

513
00:20:52,406 --> 00:20:53,975
He's 227cm,

514
00:20:54,275 --> 00:20:55,745
and is right in front of you.

515
00:20:55,845 --> 00:20:57,344
How tall are you?

516
00:20:57,345 --> 00:21:00,145
I'm 205cm now.

517
00:21:00,545 --> 00:21:03,715
He's 227cm tall, and when he raises his arms,

518
00:21:04,115 --> 00:21:06,714
- He can touch the rim. - he reaches over 3m.

519
00:21:06,715 --> 00:21:07,815
Then...

520
00:21:08,115 --> 00:21:09,284
He could score without even jumping.

521
00:21:09,285 --> 00:21:10,624
If he raised his arms in front of me,

522
00:21:10,625 --> 00:21:11,985
I wouldn't be able to see a thing.

523
00:21:14,055 --> 00:21:17,395
My gosh. I still don't understand how we could win.

524
00:21:17,865 --> 00:21:18,965
How many points did you win by?

525
00:21:19,735 --> 00:21:21,864
It was just unbelievable.

526
00:21:21,865 --> 00:21:23,735
With a minute and a half left,

527
00:21:24,105 --> 00:21:26,405
