Yes. I'm Kim Kwang Kyu, a singer of two albums.

1062
00:42:56,525 --> 00:43:00,295
We're filming in Gangneung right now.

1063
00:43:00,635 --> 00:43:02,665
- Yes. - Yes, would it...

1064
00:43:02,935 --> 00:43:05,835
be possible to film at your hotel?

1065
00:43:06,165 --> 00:43:08,505
- Do you mean today? - Pardon?

1066
00:43:08,905 --> 00:43:10,975
- Are you filming today? - Yes.

1067
00:43:12,475 --> 00:43:14,375
- What time would it be? - Pardon?

1068
00:43:14,715 --> 00:43:16,474
What time were you planning to come?

1069
00:43:16,475 --> 00:43:21,455
Between 6:30pm to 7:30pm.

1070
00:43:21,885 --> 00:43:23,085
How many people will be joining you?

1071
00:43:23,215 --> 00:43:27,655
If that would be inconvenient, we can bring fewer people.

1072
00:43:28,795 --> 00:43:32,324
If you film here,

1073
00:43:32,325 --> 00:43:36,964
what's it going to be about?

1074
00:43:36,965 --> 00:43:39,434
Oh, we're just...

1075
00:43:39,435 --> 00:43:41,974
stopping by randomly...

1076
00:43:41,975 --> 00:43:45,105
- while visiting the area. - I see.

1077
00:43:45,645 --> 00:43:48,314
We do have a reservation for 70 people in the buffet today.

1078
00:43:48,315 --> 00:43:50,414
But we'll be able to make room for you.

1079
00:43:50,415 --> 00:43:51,644
Really?

1080
00:43:51,645 --> 00:43:53,685
A buffet? Are you sure that place is to watch scenery?

1081
00:43:54,715 --> 00:43:56,814
Of course.

1082
00:43:56,815 --> 00:43:59,584
Then...

1083
00:43:59,585 --> 00:44:01,854
Ask her if we can see the scenery there.

1084
00:44:01,855 --> 00:44:03,494
- Can you hold for a second? - Yes.

1085
00:44:03,495 --> 00:44:05,294
Lee Seo Jin has something to say.

1086
00:44:05,295 --> 00:44:07,135
- Okay. - Hello.

1087
00:44:07,265 --> 00:44:09,434
- Hello. - Is it possible...

1088
00:44:09,435 --> 00:44:11,635
to get a table by the scenery?

1089
00:44:11,765 --> 00:44:14,134
- Okay. - Even if we don't eat,

1090
00:44:14,135 --> 00:44:16,505
can we still have a drink or something?

1091
00:44:17,175 --> 00:44:20,544
Oh, then do you mean when you come in...

1092
00:44:20,545 --> 00:44:22,614
you'd have tea in the lounge...

1093
00:44:22,615 --> 00:44:23,644
- Yes. - instead of a meal?

1094
00:44:23,645 --> 00:44:26,114
But I'd prefer...

1095
00:44:26,115 --> 00:44:28,215
somewhere with a nice view.

1096
00:44:28,315 --> 00:44:29,855
It doesn't have to be a restaurant.

1097
00:44:30,385 --> 00:44:32,525
Even the lobby lounge is fine.

1098
00:44:32,625 --> 00:44:34,394
- Okay. I understand. - Yes.

1099
00:44:34,395 --> 00:44:36,124
I'll check and get back to you.

1100
00:44:36,125 --> 00:44:37,665
- Thank you. Bye. - Bye.

1101
00:44:40,125 --> 00:44:42,595
I think she sounded positive.

1102
00:44:43,235 --> 00:44:45,404
(Smirking)

1103
00:44:45,405 --> 00:44:46,435
What?

1104
00:44:46,835 --> 00:44:49,174
You're turning 60 soon,

1105
00:44:49,175 --> 00:44:50,345
and is that the best you can say?

1106
00:44:52,105 --> 00:44:54,415
You said you used to work as a real estate agent.

1107
00:44:54,775 --> 00:44:56,675
That's why I never got to sign any contract.

1108
00:44:59,145 --> 00:45:00,555
I see why.

1109
00:45:01,515 --> 00:45:03,114
"Do you know My Genie Secretary?"

1110
00:45:03,115 --> 00:45:05,725
(The older bestie is high maintenance.)

1111
00:45:08,695 --> 00:45:09,695
(He got a call.)

1112
00:45:09,696 --> 00:45:10,824
- Hello? - Hello.

1113
00:45:10,825 --> 00:45:11,965
Hi.

1114
00:45:12,425 --> 00:45:17,735
(Did the hotel approve?)

1115
00:45:18,565 --> 00:45:20,034
It seems possible.

1116
00:45:20,035 --> 00:45:22,604
- Really? - You can come in at 6:30pm.

1117
00:45:22,605 --> 00:45:26,074
Yes, we'll be there...

1118
00:45:26,075 --> 00:45:28,015
by 6:30pm. Thank you.

1119
00:45:28,175 --> 00:45:30,444
- Thank you. Bye. - Bye.

1120
00:45:30,445 --> 00:45:31,885
(My Genie Secretary's mini tour)

1121
00:45:32,315 --> 00:45:33,385
Jang Hoon.

1122
00:45:34,655 --> 00:45:35,655
Jang Hoon.

1123
00:45:37,355 --> 00:45:38,555
- Jang Hoon. - They look the same.

1124
00:45:39,025 --> 00:45:40,055
They look the same.

1125
00:45:40,695 --> 00:45:41,695
(Did you call me?)

1126
00:45:41,696 --> 00:45:42,855
I agree.

1127
00:45:44,395 --> 00:45:45,565
They have the same eyes, don't they?

1128
00:45:46,425 --> 00:45:49,494
(Eyes just as cute as My Star's)

1129
00:45:49,495 --> 00:45:51,404
Jang Hoon.

1130
00:45:51,405 --> 00:45:52,535
Yes.

1131
00:45:54,175 --> 00:45:56,175
(Standing up)

1132
00:45:57,205 --> 00:45:58,274
(My Star suddenly appears.)

1133
00:45:58,275 --> 00:45:59,704
- He's done. - I'm done.

1134
00:45:59,705 --> 00:46:00,874
- He's done. - Are you done?

1135
00:46:00,875 --> 00:46:02,114
- Yes. - Let's move.

1136
00:46:02,115 --> 00:46:05,484
We're going to the gallery now.

1137
00:46:05,485 --> 00:46:07,084
- Are we moving now? - Yes.

1138
00:46:07,085 --> 00:46:09,684
Have you been monitoring?

1139
00:46:09,685 --> 00:46:11,284
We have.

1140
00:46:11,285 --> 00:46:12,624
Then we left when you were drawing.

1141
00:46:12,625 --> 00:46:14,824
When I was drawing? Was there anything that stood out...

1142
00:46:14,825 --> 00:46:15,895
until then?

1143
00:46:18,095 --> 00:46:20,294
(My Star's sharp question)

1144
00:46:20,295 --> 00:46:24,305
- It's perfect. - It's perfect.

1145
00:46:24,435 --> 00:46:27,474
- Yes. - If there's any problem,

1146
00:46:27,475 --> 00:46:29,204
- it's all your fault. - Never.

1147
00:46:29,205 --> 00:46:30,275
There will never be a problem.

1148
00:46:31,675 --> 00:46:32,844
I've said...

1149
00:46:32,845 --> 00:46:34,645
(Jumping)

1150
00:46:36,775 --> 00:46:37,984
- There's a bug. - Okay.

1151
00:46:37,985 --> 00:46:40,145
(A bug on My neat Star?)

1152
00:46:42,355 --> 00:46:44,354
- There really is one. - A bug.

1153
00:46:44,355 --> 00:46:46,085
Bend down. He can't reach it.

1154
00:46:46,125 --> 00:46:47,695
- A spider? - Hey, you do it.

1155
00:46:48,125 --> 00:46:50,694
(Restless after seeing a bug 2m high)

1156
00:46:50,695 --> 00:46:52,265
Bend down. He can't reach it.

1157
00:46:52,795 --> 00:46:53,865
(Blowing)

1158
00:46:54,165 --> 00:46:55,294
(Aiming)

1159
00:46:55,295 --> 00:46:57,565
(Neatly removing the bug)

1160
00:46:58,135 --> 00:46:59,865
- You hit it like this. - Okay.

1161
00:47:00,875 --> 00:47:02,634
It was on your head.

1162
00:47:02,635 --> 00:47:03,635
So...

1163
00:47:03,636 --> 00:47:04,804
it's over after one lap.

1164
00:47:04,805 --> 00:47:06,204
- It's only this big. - So?

1165
00:47:06,205 --> 00:47:07,415
Are you going to wash your hands or not?

1166
00:47:09,345 --> 00:47:10,545
Oh, that's...

1167
00:47:10,715 --> 00:47:13,344
(My Star got ink on his hands while drawing.)

1168
00:47:13,345 --> 00:47:15,015
The wet wipe won't do it.

1169
00:47:15,255 --> 00:47:17,154
(What's it going to be?)

1170
00:47:17,155 --> 00:47:18,655
Go wash your hands in the restroom.

1171
00:47:19,385 --> 00:47:21,125
Let me think about it.

1172
00:47:21,555 --> 00:47:22,695
Okay.

1173
00:47:23,625 --> 00:47:24,724
Did you touch something?

1174
00:47:24,725 --> 00:47:26,494
I don't like to use restrooms outside.

1175
00:47:26,495 --> 00:47:28,534
- As much as possible. - That's ink.

1176
00:47:28,535 --> 00:47:30,564
But it was pretty clean.

1177
00:47:30,565 --> 00:47:32,004
I'm okay so far.

1178
00:47:32,005 --> 00:47:34,134
There was soap too.

1179
00:47:34,135 --> 00:47:36,175
(My Star's down.)

1180
00:47:36,435 --> 00:47:38,405
(On eggshells)

1181
00:47:39,375 --> 00:47:40,404
I'll wait for you in the car.

1182
00:47:40,405 --> 00:47:42,975
(Moving)

1183
00:47:43,615 --> 00:47:46,985
(Seo Genie gets in the driver's seat.)

1184
00:47:50,785 --> 00:47:55,025
(Setting the optimal indoor temperature)

1185
00:47:57,125 --> 00:48:00,024
(Next)

1186
00:48:00,025 --> 00:48:04,735
(Grabbing the schedule)

1187
00:48:05,735 --> 00:48:09,035
(Setting the GPS)

1188
00:48:09,905 --> 00:48:12,675
(Kwang Kyu is waiting to serve My Star.)

1189
00:48:13,805 --> 00:48:16,775
(Spotting the Lord)

1190
00:48:17,045 --> 00:48:19,015
- See you. - Nice to meet you.

1191
00:48:19,385 --> 00:48:20,615
See you soon.

1192
00:48:22,415 --> 00:48:25,955
(Bowing at their backs)

1193
00:48:27,755 --> 00:48:30,965
(The Lord appears.)

1194
00:48:31,995 --> 00:48:32,995
(Dashing)

1195
00:48:33,565 --> 00:48:34,894
- Let's go. - Let's go.

1196
00:48:34,895 --> 00:48:36,765
(Serving before My Star gets upset)

1197
00:48:37,095 --> 00:48:39,535
- You should go the other way. - I'm only opening the door for you.

1198
00:48:40,535 --> 00:48:42,234
- My Star. - You don't have to do that.

1199
00:48:42,235 --> 00:48:44,544
I have to.

1200
00:48:44,545 --> 00:48:46,674
- You don't have to do that. - It's my job.

1201
00:48:46,675 --> 00:48:48,144
- Gosh. - Oh, gosh.

1202
00:48:48,145 --> 00:48:50,214
- Thank you. - You're welcome.

1203
00:48:50,215 --> 00:48:51,215
(Setting off in good mood)

1204
00:48:54,915 --> 00:48:58,055
(Silence in the car)

1205
00:48:59,125 --> 00:49:00,725
(Glancing)

1206
00:49:01,155 --> 00:49:02,355
(Glancing)

1207
00:49:02,525 --> 00:49:07,025
(When he's down, show him cute videos or pirctures.)

1208
00:49:07,295 --> 00:49:10,195
I heard you like to see babies when you're tired.

1209
00:49:10,335 --> 00:49:12,804
- Babies... - Who is that?

1210
00:49:12,805 --> 00:49:13,805
Babies...

1211
00:49:13,806 --> 00:49:15,274
(Good job, Kwang Kyu.)

1212
00:49:15,275 --> 00:49:19,104
My friend had a housewarming party the other day.

1213
00:49:19,105 --> 00:49:21,544
His youngest is so cute.

1214
00:49:21,545 --> 00:49:23,045
(Playing a cute video)

1215
00:49:23,645 --> 00:49:25,385
(Laughing)

1216
00:49:25,515 --> 00:49:28,255
He got food all over his clothes.

1217
00:49:29,185 --> 00:49:31,225
Look at what he's doing.

1218
00:49:31,855 --> 00:49:32,925
Gosh.

1219
00:49:34,325 --> 00:49:38,765
I wish I had a child.

1220
00:49:38,865 --> 00:49:41,235
- Don't you? - Yes.

1221
00:49:45,765 --> 00:49:47,905
(Glancing)

1222
00:49:48,175 --> 00:49:49,505
Do you have a nephew or a niece?

1223
00:49:49,875 --> 00:49:52,274
I do. I have...

1224
00:49:52,275 --> 00:49:54,515
two nieces.

1225
00:49:55,275 --> 00:49:57,545
But we're not that close.

1226
00:49:57,985 --> 00:50:00,184
(The doting uncle feels bad for him.)

1227
00:50:00,185 --> 00:50:03,815
They went to study in Canada after going to middle school.

1228
00:50:04,485 --> 00:50:06,624
- You don't get to see them often. - No.

1229
00:50:06,625 --> 00:50:09,525
The oldest got into UCLA.

1230
00:50:09,955 --> 00:50:14,735
The youngest is going to college this year.

1231
00:50:15,565 --> 00:50:17,564
I don't get to see them. They're abroad.

1232
00:50:17,565 --> 00:50:18,765
(Coy)

1233
00:50:19,035 --> 00:50:20,434
You should get married soon.

1234
00:50:20,435 --> 00:50:23,135
(The conversation ends with marriage.)

1235
00:50:23,675 --> 00:50:24,745
Here we are.

1236
00:50:24,975 --> 00:50:26,374
Is this the gallery?

1237
00:50:26,375 --> 00:50:28,414
(5pm, Haslla Art World)

1238
00:50:28,415 --> 00:50:29,974
It's bigger than I thought.

1239
00:50:29,975 --> 00:50:32,815
(It's about 109,090m² wide.)

1240
00:50:34,055 --> 00:50:35,055
(There are terrific sculptures everywhere.)

1241
00:50:35,056 --> 00:50:36,355
That's a cool sculpture.

1242
00:50:37,285 --> 00:50:38,785
Check this out.

1243
00:50:39,185 --> 00:50:42,525
It's huge.

1244
00:50:42,595 --> 00:50:43,854
It's cool.

1245
00:50:43,855 --> 00:50:45,095
Look at the boat.

1246
00:50:46,225 --> 00:50:47,325
- It's incredible. - Look at that.

1247
00:50:48,695 --> 00:50:49,695
The sea...

1248
00:50:50,835 --> 00:50:52,804
(Exclaiming)

1249
00:50:52,805 --> 00:50:53,805
Awesome.

1250
00:50:55,505 --> 00:50:57,444
It's basically floating in the sea.

1251
00:50:57,445 --> 00:50:58,905
(What surprised My Star?)

1252
00:50:58,975 --> 00:51:01,914
- Oh, what is that? - That's Jeongdongjin.

1253
00:51:01,915 --> 00:51:03,074
I know.

1254
00:51:03,075 --> 00:51:04,345
This is amazing.

1255
00:51:05,985 --> 00:51:07,314
(Before My Star's eyes...)

1256
00:51:07,315 --> 00:51:08,655
This is awesome.

1257
00:51:09,285 --> 00:51:11,984
(lies the endless Gangneung sea.)

1258
00:51:11,985 --> 00:51:13,755
This place is awesome.

1259
00:51:14,925 --> 00:51:18,494
(The East Sea clears your mind just by looking at it.)

1260
00:51:18,495 --> 00:51:19,525
Awesome.

1261
00:51:21,835 --> 00:51:23,834
- Awesome. - Awesome.

1262
00:51:23,835 --> 00:51:24,964
I'm scared.

1263
00:51:24,965 --> 00:51:26,405
(The beautiful sight excites My Star.)

1264
00:51:28,205 --> 00:51:31,145
I didn't expect to see this view at all.

1265
00:51:31,605 --> 00:51:33,605
This is unimaginable.

1266
00:51:33,675 --> 00:51:35,245
This place is the best.

1267
00:51:35,775 --> 00:51:39,115
When I was 7 or 8,

1268
00:51:39,385 --> 00:51:42,515
Gyeongpodae was the first place my family visited on a trip.

1269
00:51:43,215 --> 00:51:45,384
It means so much to me.

1270
00:51:45,385 --> 00:51:47,154
I think this is the first time...

1271
00:51:47,155 --> 00:51:48,424
(Back to Gangneung after 44 years)

1272
00:51:48,425 --> 00:51:49,625
after eight.

1273
00:51:50,655 --> 00:51:51,895
It feels like I'm abroad.

1274
00:51:52,095 --> 00:51:54,064
- Hey. - You know?

1275
00:51:54,065 --> 00:51:55,494
It's worth coming here.

1276
00:51:55,495 --> 00:51:56,694
It feels like I'm abroad.

1277
00:51:56,695 --> 00:51:59,165
(My Star is back to 8.)

1278
00:51:59,765 --> 00:52:02,335
I could only see this in Hawaii or...

1279
00:52:02,835 --> 00:52:04,845
This is even better than Hawaii.

1280
00:52:05,205 --> 00:52:08,515
I haven't seen such a wide view like this.

1281
00:52:11,115 --> 00:52:13,814
This is basically the Pacific Ocean, isn't it?

1282
00:52:13,815 --> 00:52:14,985
It is.

1283
00:52:17,215 --> 00:52:19,425
I couldn't believe...

1284
00:52:20,125 --> 00:52:23,724
I could see such a vast ocean...

1285
00:52:23,725 --> 00:52:26,465
in the country.

1286
00:52:26,795 --> 00:52:28,434
I got a lot on my mind.

1287
00:52:28,435 --> 00:52:30,534
I thought...

1288
00:52:30,535 --> 00:52:34,275
I should see something like this more often.

1289
00:52:34,605 --> 00:52:38,605
I was very happy.

1290
00:52:40,405 --> 00:52:41,775
This place is...

1291
00:52:42,245 --> 00:52:46,215
(The wonderful sight made My Star speechless.)

1292
00:52:47,185 --> 00:52:48,954
(Don't forget to take pictures.)

1293
00:52:48,955 --> 00:52:50,115
Right. Pictures.

1294
00:52:51,085 --> 00:52:52,584
(My Genie Secretary's official photographer)

1295
00:52:52,585 --> 00:52:53,784
My Star.

1296
00:52:53,785 --> 00:52:55,854
(Thumbs up)

1297
00:52:55,855 --> 00:52:58,724
(2m-tall boy giant)

1298
00:52:58,725 --> 00:53:00,595
- Give me the camera. - No, let's take it together.

1299
00:53:01,195 --> 00:53:02,395
One, two, three.

1300
00:53:02,765 --> 00:53:05,565
(This is the romantic height difference.)

1301
00:53:05,805 --> 00:53:06,865
Let me take your picture.

1302
00:53:07,805 --> 00:53:09,775
- Go stand. - Thank you.

1303
00:53:10,435 --> 00:53:13,275
(He likes unique poses.)

1304
00:53:14,075 --> 00:53:16,075
(Polite legs)

1305
00:53:16,115 --> 00:53:19,215
(I'll be a millionaire one day.)

1306
00:53:19,385 --> 00:53:21,715
- Cool. - It's incredible.

1307
00:53:22,715 --> 00:53:24,355
- It's the best. - It's wonderful.

1308
00:53:24,855 --> 00:53:26,555
You really are rich.

1309
00:53:27,025 --> 00:53:28,225
Hey.

1310
00:53:28,555 --> 00:53:30,524
- He's even richer than you are. - Oh, no.

1311
00:53:30,525 --> 00:53:32,865
- I'm nothing. - True.

1312
00:53:33,395 --> 00:53:34,395
(The place that touches My Star...)

1313
00:53:34,396 --> 00:53:35,534
I'm jealous.

1314
00:53:35,535 --> 00:53:37,935
(and makes him modest at the same time)

1315
00:53:39,265 --> 00:53:40,874
You can face outside.

1316
00:53:40,875 --> 00:53:42,575
(Seo Jin found a place to wait.)

1317
00:53:43,075 --> 00:53:44,105
This way.

1318
00:53:44,605 --> 00:53:45,804
- It's crazy. - What?

1319
00:53:45,805 --> 00:53:47,304
- I love this place. - The view is...

1320
00:53:47,305 --> 00:53:49,814
It's all gallery outside.

1321
00:53:49,815 --> 00:53:52,015
It's 495,867m²...

1322
00:53:52,785 --> 00:53:57,185
(My Star bumps into the light.)

1323
00:53:57,985 --> 00:54:02,095
(Watch out for My Star's height.)

1324
00:54:02,525 --> 00:54:04,564
It's 495,867m²...

1325
00:54:04,565 --> 00:54:05,924
Oh, no.

1326
00:54:05,925 --> 00:54:08,165
- Hey. - It scared me.

1327
00:54:08,795 --> 00:54:09,864
Hey.

1328
00:54:09,865 --> 00:54:11,404
Hey. Gosh.

1329
00:54:11,405 --> 00:54:12,905
- I can't believe you touched it. - But...

1330
00:54:13,005 --> 00:54:14,064
I can't believe you touched it.

1331
