1463
00:59:18,805 --> 00:59:21,675
Jang Hoon knows a lot about history.

1464
00:59:21,745 --> 00:59:23,614
After Ojukheon House?

1465
00:59:23,615 --> 00:59:24,615
Then...

1466
00:59:24,616 --> 00:59:27,785
the best hotel in Gyeongpodae is S Hotel.

1467
00:59:28,655 --> 00:59:29,784
Isn't that place known...

1468
00:59:29,785 --> 00:59:30,884
- for the view? - It's the best.

1469
00:59:30,885 --> 00:59:32,625
Because it's standing on the cliff.

1470
00:59:32,685 --> 00:59:34,025
We'll have...

1471
00:59:34,125 --> 00:59:36,395
drinks there...

1472
00:59:37,195 --> 00:59:38,595
and enjoy the view.

1473
00:59:38,795 --> 00:59:39,864
And...

1474
00:59:39,865 --> 00:59:42,034
the sashimi restaurant I went in my 20s is...

1475
00:59:42,035 --> 00:59:43,595
still around.

1476
00:59:43,735 --> 00:59:46,404
In Gyeongpodae.

1477
00:59:46,405 --> 00:59:48,174
It's known...

1478
00:59:48,175 --> 00:59:51,845
to be a favorite of former presidents and chairmen.

1479
00:59:51,875 --> 00:59:53,104
That's how it's known.

1480
00:59:53,105 --> 00:59:54,144
Really?

1481
00:59:54,145 --> 00:59:55,814
When they're not actually open today?

1482
00:59:55,815 --> 00:59:57,014
They weren't going to open today.

1483
00:59:57,015 --> 00:59:58,444
That's amazing.

1484
00:59:58,445 --> 00:59:59,814
(Today's course)

1485
00:59:59,815 --> 01:00:01,185
(Ojukheon House, Gyeongpodae, sashimi restaurant)

1486
01:00:01,285 --> 01:00:03,985
I'm getting high expectations.

1487
01:00:04,625 --> 01:00:06,855
(You may look forward to it.)

1488
01:00:06,925 --> 01:00:08,294
(Ojukheon House, Gyeongpo Lake, current location)

1489
01:00:08,295 --> 01:00:09,524
(S Hotel)

1490
01:00:09,525 --> 01:00:12,025
(Sashimi Restaurant)

1491
01:00:13,095 --> 01:00:15,995
(Staring)

1492
01:00:18,105 --> 01:00:22,805
(He can't stop looking outside.)

1493
01:00:23,805 --> 01:00:25,375
This place has...

1494
01:00:26,405 --> 01:00:27,644
a magnificent view.

1495
01:00:27,645 --> 01:00:28,845
It's wonderful.

1496
01:00:29,445 --> 01:00:31,845
- Right here. - It's nice.

1497
01:00:32,445 --> 01:00:35,355
I get to check out Gangneung.

1498
01:00:36,715 --> 01:00:37,884
It's nice.

1499
01:00:37,885 --> 01:00:38,925
(Rolling down the window)

1500
01:00:40,485 --> 01:00:42,124
It's a good place for a honeymoon.

1501
01:00:42,125 --> 01:00:44,424
(The autumn Gangneung sea catches My Star's attention.)

1502
01:00:44,425 --> 01:00:45,665
Look at the sea.

1503
01:00:47,795 --> 01:00:50,364
There's a seawall at the end.

1504
01:00:50,365 --> 01:00:51,734
I see a lighthouse.

1505
01:00:51,735 --> 01:00:53,435
There's everything.

1506
01:00:54,705 --> 01:00:57,775
Does it lead to downtown?

1507
01:00:58,475 --> 01:01:00,505
We're heading to Gangneung.

1508
01:01:01,775 --> 01:01:03,474
We're near Gangneung.

1509
01:01:03,475 --> 01:01:05,184
- From Jeongdongjin? - That's right.

1510
01:01:05,185 --> 01:01:07,344
(They're near downtown Gangneung.)

1511
01:01:07,345 --> 01:01:09,915
This must be downtown, right?

1512
01:01:10,085 --> 01:01:11,584
- This is totally... - This is...

1513
01:01:11,585 --> 01:01:12,825
- my first time coming here. - Really?

1514
01:01:13,025 --> 01:01:14,694
- You had no chance to come. - Aside from...

1515
01:01:14,695 --> 01:01:17,624
visiting Gyeongpodae with my family...

1516
01:01:17,625 --> 01:01:19,694
when I was young...

1517
01:01:19,695 --> 01:01:20,794
- Gyeongpodae. - Isn't that way too long ago?

1518
01:01:20,795 --> 01:01:22,034
When you were eight?

1519
01:01:22,035 --> 01:01:23,565
- When I was eight. - That was so long ago.

1520
01:01:24,195 --> 01:01:27,204
All I remember is Gyeongpodae when I was eight.

1521
01:01:27,205 --> 01:01:28,835
(Redrawing his memories of Gangneung when he was 8)

1522
01:01:29,775 --> 01:01:30,904
- Hey. That's... - That's cool.

1523
01:01:30,905 --> 01:01:32,005
What is that?

1524
01:01:32,805 --> 01:01:34,205
- There's all kinds of stuff. - What is that?

1525
01:01:34,715 --> 01:01:36,744
- What is this place? - That's cool. What's that?

1526
01:01:36,745 --> 01:01:38,014
It's a fishing area.

1527
01:01:38,015 --> 01:01:40,015
It's not a fishing area. It looks like a cafe.

1528
01:01:40,445 --> 01:01:42,014
- It looks like a cafe. - I think...

1529
01:01:42,015 --> 01:01:44,515
you can eat there on the water.

1530
01:01:44,615 --> 01:01:46,385
It keeps changing.

1531
01:01:46,485 --> 01:01:49,395
It says luna in Spanish.

1532
01:01:50,195 --> 01:01:52,664
I think it's a floating cafe.

1533
01:01:52,665 --> 01:01:54,734
In the middle...

1534
01:01:54,735 --> 01:01:55,794
What's inside the ball?

1535
01:01:55,795 --> 01:01:57,094
I think it's a park.

1536
01:01:57,095 --> 01:01:59,205
- What is that? - That's cool.

1537
01:02:00,565 --> 01:02:05,005
I visited it when I was really young.

1538
01:02:05,645 --> 01:02:08,145
Everything looked fascinating after so long.

1539
01:02:09,675 --> 01:02:11,684
(While driving here and there,)

1540
01:02:11,685 --> 01:02:15,715
(it became dark.)

1541
01:02:16,985 --> 01:02:19,285
It's pretty late.

1542
01:02:19,585 --> 01:02:22,925
I think we'll have to see Ojukheon House...

1543
01:02:23,425 --> 01:02:25,695
in the car.

1544
01:02:25,965 --> 01:02:27,565
I think we'll just pass by.

1545
01:02:27,725 --> 01:02:29,034
Then...

1546
01:02:29,035 --> 01:02:31,034
why don't you tell us about Ojukheon House?

1547
01:02:31,035 --> 01:02:33,804
Since you know a lot about history.

1548
01:02:33,805 --> 01:02:37,204
You know...

1549
01:02:37,205 --> 01:02:39,145
that's where Yi Yul Gok was born, right?

1550
01:02:39,305 --> 01:02:41,875
Yes. That's about all I know.

1551
01:02:42,015 --> 01:02:45,885
That is Shin Saimdang's...

1552
01:02:46,015 --> 01:02:48,215
parents' house.

1553
01:02:48,655 --> 01:02:52,154
I think when she got pregnant...

1554
01:02:52,155 --> 01:02:54,024
with Yi Yul Gok...

1555
01:02:54,025 --> 01:02:55,995
- She gave birth. - She gave birth there.

1556
01:02:56,355 --> 01:02:59,195
It's the only family in this country...

1557
01:02:59,265 --> 01:03:00,994
to have two members...

1558
01:03:00,995 --> 01:03:02,294
appear in the banknotes.

1559
01:03:02,295 --> 01:03:03,964
(Mother and son in the banknotes are unprecedented in the world.)

1560
01:03:03,965 --> 01:03:05,205
(Building historical knowledge)

1561
01:03:05,335 --> 01:03:07,404
All you need to see in Ojukheon House is...

1562
01:03:07,405 --> 01:03:10,175
the black bamboos.

1563
01:03:10,535 --> 01:03:12,905
(Excited to see black bamboos)

1564
01:03:15,075 --> 01:03:16,214
It's Ojukheon House.

1565
01:03:16,215 --> 01:03:17,475
(Arriving in Ojukheon House even before they know it)

1566
01:03:17,715 --> 01:03:18,885
Oh, Ojukheon House.

1567
01:03:19,015 --> 01:03:20,815
So this is Ojukheon House.

1568
01:03:21,285 --> 01:03:23,585
(Excited)

1569
01:03:24,755 --> 01:03:28,454
(Looking around)

1570
01:03:28,455 --> 01:03:29,795
When did it get this big?

1571
01:03:29,925 --> 01:03:31,625
- It's huge. - The place...

1572
01:03:31,695 --> 01:03:33,065
It's really big inside.

1573
01:03:33,665 --> 01:03:37,295
I don't remember there being gates and all in the past.

1574
01:03:37,435 --> 01:03:40,105
Was the house always this big?

1575
01:03:40,435 --> 01:03:42,175
I mean during the Joseon dynasty.

1576
01:03:43,205 --> 01:03:44,634
It's huge.

1577
01:03:44,635 --> 01:03:47,275
It's big, and the inside is much bigger.

1578
01:03:48,105 --> 01:03:50,345
Are we inside a military headquarters?

1579
01:03:51,245 --> 01:03:53,544
My gosh, look at the size of the gate.

1580
01:03:53,545 --> 01:03:55,615
(Looking around will take some time.)

1581
01:03:57,385 --> 01:03:58,425
Wait.

1582
01:03:58,925 --> 01:03:59,955
What is it?

1583
01:04:00,225 --> 01:04:02,394
(It's closed.)

1584
01:04:02,395 --> 01:04:03,625
It's blocked.

1585
01:04:03,795 --> 01:04:04,825
What?

1586
01:04:07,195 --> 01:04:09,535
(Walking on eggshells)

1587
01:04:10,065 --> 01:04:11,295
Ojukheon House is closed.

1588
01:04:11,505 --> 01:04:12,665
(Walking on eggshells)

1589
01:04:13,235 --> 01:04:15,305
We can't take a look inside.

1590
01:04:15,375 --> 01:04:17,305
(Closed for the day)

