1948
01:17:49,015 --> 01:17:50,085
Delicious.

1949
01:17:52,525 --> 01:17:53,525
With this?

1950
01:17:54,785 --> 01:17:56,295
- It's good. - It's really good.

1951
01:17:56,595 --> 01:17:58,625
You have to eat it warm for the best flavor.

1952
01:17:58,955 --> 01:18:00,025
It's really good.

1953
01:18:01,525 --> 01:18:02,795
You sure are digging in.

1954
01:18:03,435 --> 01:18:05,665
You look happy, Jang Hoon.

1955
01:18:06,605 --> 01:18:08,805
(I'm glad I brought you here.)

1956
01:18:10,875 --> 01:18:12,035
Today...

1957
01:18:12,475 --> 01:18:13,504
It's good.

1958
01:18:13,505 --> 01:18:16,214
I'm really being spoiled thanks to My Genie Secretary.

1959
01:18:16,215 --> 01:18:17,614
Totally.

1960
01:18:17,615 --> 01:18:19,945
I haven't had snow crabs in years, you know?

1961
01:18:20,745 --> 01:18:22,355
- Really? What a surprise. - For real?

1962
01:18:22,815 --> 01:18:24,154
- Seriously. - My gosh.

1963
01:18:24,155 --> 01:18:26,025
I only ever got deliveries.

1964
01:18:27,655 --> 01:18:28,855
What do you usually order?

1965
01:18:29,325 --> 01:18:30,455
You know just...

1966
01:18:31,525 --> 01:18:34,495
- Jjajangmyeon, - Oh, dear.

1967
01:18:34,795 --> 01:18:35,965
kimchi stew,

1968
01:18:36,395 --> 01:18:38,465
and sundae soup. It's one of those three.

1969
01:18:39,965 --> 01:18:41,534
- You're happy, right? - Yes.

1970
01:18:41,535 --> 01:18:44,005
(My Star is very happy today.)

1971
01:18:45,845 --> 01:18:46,975
Give me a bit more chojang.

1972
01:18:49,575 --> 01:18:52,345
(Taking care of the Young Master)

1973
01:18:53,215 --> 01:18:56,285
(Staring)

1974
01:18:56,855 --> 01:18:59,624
Kwang Kyu takes more care of...

1975
01:18:59,625 --> 01:19:01,355
Seo Jin than me.

1976
01:19:02,525 --> 01:19:03,995
That just now was a shocker.

1977
01:19:04,995 --> 01:19:06,694
(Taking care of the Young Master has become second nature.)

1978
01:19:06,695 --> 01:19:08,165
You see...

1979
01:19:10,095 --> 01:19:11,235
That just now was a shocker.

1980
01:19:12,065 --> 01:19:15,605
Watching Kwang Kyu fill up Seo Jin's chojang dish...

1981
01:19:15,975 --> 01:19:17,434
shocked me.

1982
01:19:17,435 --> 01:19:19,945
- Isn't today's My Star me? - It is.

1983
01:19:20,845 --> 01:19:22,915
He takes more care of Seo Jin than me.

1984
01:19:23,675 --> 01:19:26,014
Here's the commanding system.

1985
01:19:26,015 --> 01:19:28,744
When Jang Hoon gives me an order, I pass that on to Kwang Kyu.

1986
01:19:28,745 --> 01:19:30,314
That's the system.

1987
01:19:30,315 --> 01:19:31,755
It's how my life has always been.

1988
01:19:35,855 --> 01:19:39,725
(I should dig in to take care of Seo Jin.)

1989
01:19:42,665 --> 01:19:44,165
Kwang Kyu, you must love crabs.

1990
01:19:44,435 --> 01:19:46,964
- Of course. - It's really good eaten warm.

1991
01:19:46,965 --> 01:19:49,205
It's best when it's warm.

1992
01:19:49,605 --> 01:19:50,775
It's delicious.

1993
01:19:52,275 --> 01:19:53,704
(An advanced skill)

1994
01:19:53,705 --> 01:19:55,844
What's gotten into him?

1995
01:19:55,845 --> 01:19:57,315
(Munching)

1996
01:19:57,745 --> 01:20:00,015
- Me? - Are you in your andropause?

1997
01:20:01,145 --> 01:20:03,054
I'm in my andropause throughout the year.

1998
01:20:03,055 --> 01:20:04,155
(All year round)

1999
01:20:04,385 --> 01:20:06,024
I've been in my andropause since birth.

2000
01:20:06,025 --> 01:20:07,124
(Andropause symptoms: Decreased testosterone...)

2001
01:20:07,125 --> 01:20:08,324
(can increase appetite and lead to weight gain)

2002
01:20:08,325 --> 01:20:10,495
- I'm curious. - Are you not in your andropause?

2003
01:20:11,255 --> 01:20:14,164
Seo Jin is really cranky because it's hit him.

2004
01:20:14,165 --> 01:20:16,835
I'm not in my andropause yet.

2005
01:20:17,765 --> 01:20:19,835
It's just that...

2006
01:20:20,435 --> 01:20:24,235
I get a little sad at times since I've been single for so long.

2007
01:20:24,705 --> 01:20:25,875
That's andropause.

2008
01:20:28,575 --> 01:20:29,615
Are you lonely?

2009
01:20:30,245 --> 01:20:32,615
I'm not that lonely.

2010
01:20:32,985 --> 01:20:35,184
It's kind of different.

2011
01:20:35,185 --> 01:20:37,154
I'm not lonely because I don't have anyone by my side.

2012
01:20:37,155 --> 01:20:38,515
Exactly. That's andropause.

2013
01:20:40,855 --> 01:20:42,124
- That's andropause. - Really?

2014
01:20:42,125 --> 01:20:43,624
It's not because you're single.

2015
01:20:43,625 --> 01:20:45,494
Andropause has hit the two together.

2016
01:20:45,495 --> 01:20:47,494
I'm not lonely because I'm single.

2017
01:20:47,495 --> 01:20:48,624
Why am I...

2018
01:20:48,625 --> 01:20:50,964
- How much longer will I... - Anxiety and impatience...

2019
01:20:50,965 --> 01:20:52,865
- come rushing in. - Yes.

2020
01:20:53,405 --> 01:20:54,435
There's no reason behind it.

2021
01:20:55,605 --> 01:20:57,975
You become anxious and impatient for no reason.

2022
01:20:58,405 --> 01:21:00,304
- That's andropause. - What about this?

2023
01:21:00,305 --> 01:21:04,415
What about thoughts like, "Won't it get lonelier..."

2024
01:21:05,260 --> 01:21:07,400
"without anyone the more I grow older?"

2025
01:21:08,585 --> 01:21:10,015
That doesn't cross my mind.

2026
01:21:12,525 --> 01:21:15,724
Things like, "How nice would it be if someone greeted me at home?"

2027
01:21:15,725 --> 01:21:17,594
- No. - I love it...

2028
01:21:17,595 --> 01:21:19,565
when I enter my pitch dark house.

2029
01:21:20,765 --> 01:21:22,425
I don't like a lit up house.

2030
01:21:22,795 --> 01:21:26,204
He and I are on the same page on that.

2031
01:21:26,205 --> 01:21:27,334
(What the men have in common)

2032
01:21:27,335 --> 01:21:28,834
But the lights should be on.

2033
01:21:28,835 --> 01:21:30,674
I hate it when my house is dark.

2034
01:21:30,675 --> 01:21:32,335
When the lights are on, I'm like,

2035
01:21:32,575 --> 01:21:34,244
- "What?" - Don't you get anxious?

2036
01:21:34,245 --> 01:21:35,644
- Right? - Is it a thief?

2037
01:21:35,645 --> 01:21:38,775
"Did a thief break in?"

2038
01:21:39,515 --> 01:21:41,615
Say that I forgot to turn them off when I left.

2039
01:21:42,345 --> 01:21:43,955
"Oh, no. The electricity bills."

2040
01:21:46,055 --> 01:21:48,384
I'm fine with paying for a 1,000 dollar get-together meal.

2041
01:21:48,385 --> 01:21:49,624
Totally.

2042
01:21:49,625 --> 01:21:52,765
But it's a different story when it comes to using...

2043
01:21:53,425 --> 01:21:56,265
unnecessary energy at home.

2044
01:21:57,935 --> 01:21:59,305
The rich are worse.

2045
01:22:00,405 --> 01:22:02,835
(The frugal ones)

2046
01:22:03,605 --> 01:22:06,344
I recently splurged.

2047
01:22:06,345 --> 01:22:09,145
I changed my fridge.

2048
01:22:09,675 --> 01:22:11,575
- My kitchen is small. - I see.

2049
01:22:12,415 --> 01:22:14,145
I found this chicken fit.

2050
01:22:15,515 --> 01:22:17,185
I found this chicken fit.

2051
01:22:17,815 --> 01:22:20,454
- Kitchen fit? - Yes, kitchen fit.

2052
01:22:20,455 --> 01:22:22,154
Kwang Kyu just said chicken fit.

2053
01:22:22,155 --> 01:22:24,124
- Exactly. I thought I misheard him. - My bad.

2054
01:22:24,125 --> 01:22:27,265
I thought it was chicken feet when he said chicken fit.

2055
01:22:27,565 --> 01:22:29,564
- You mean your new house, right? - Yes.

2056
01:22:29,565 --> 01:22:31,194
Yes, I bought a kitchen fit.

2057
01:22:31,195 --> 01:22:33,765
The kitchen fit was more expensive than I imagined.

2058
01:22:34,305 --> 01:22:35,365
- How much was it? - It was a big decision.

2059
01:22:35,665 --> 01:22:37,635
It was around 3,200 dollars.

2060
01:22:40,545 --> 01:22:41,804
You didn't buy anything recently, did you?

2061
01:22:41,805 --> 01:22:43,475
(What's My Star's most recent purchase?)

2062
01:22:44,415 --> 01:22:46,384
- You don't buy things, do you? - Is it a building?

2063
01:22:46,385 --> 01:22:47,385
A building?

2064
01:22:47,386 --> 01:22:50,054
- A building is unbeatable. - No.

2065
01:22:50,055 --> 01:22:51,415
I can't remember what I bought.

2066
01:22:52,555 --> 01:22:56,324
(What did I buy again?)

2067
01:22:56,325 --> 01:22:57,455
Be honest about it.

2068
01:22:57,995 --> 01:23:00,295
But really, maybe he didn't buy anything.

2069
01:23:02,840 --> 01:23:04,910
- I bought squid. - Oh, my.

2070
01:23:05,780 --> 01:23:07,079
Did you buy a squid-catching boat?

2071
01:23:07,080 --> 01:23:08,509
From home shopping...

2072
01:23:08,510 --> 01:23:09,979
- Squid? - Why did you buy squid?

2073
01:23:09,980 --> 01:23:11,180
Half-dried!

2074
01:23:11,880 --> 01:23:13,220
I almost bought it.

2075
01:23:13,320 --> 01:23:14,479
I bought it.

2076
01:23:14,480 --> 01:23:16,420
You don't grill it at home, do you?

2077
01:23:16,450 --> 01:23:17,919
It said I didn't have to.

2078
01:23:17,920 --> 01:23:19,090
Exactly, we don't.

2079
01:23:19,590 --> 01:23:21,559
- Open it, and eat it as is. - I knew it.

2080
01:23:21,560 --> 01:23:23,530
Jang Hoon isn't the type to do things at home.

2081
01:23:23,660 --> 01:23:25,160
Okay, fine.

2082
01:23:25,190 --> 01:23:27,500
I bought squid, okay?

2083
01:23:27,600 --> 01:23:29,599
That's cute. Buying squid was cute.

2084
01:23:29,600 --> 01:23:30,630
Squid.

2085
01:23:31,870 --> 01:23:34,870
Jang Hoon, aren't you on many anger-inducing shows?

2086
01:23:35,370 --> 01:23:37,709
How do you usually keep yourself calm?

2087
01:23:37,710 --> 01:23:39,579
(How does My Star calm himself?)

2088
01:23:39,580 --> 01:23:40,709
You do an unusual number of...

2089
01:23:40,710 --> 01:23:41,879
- anger-inducing shows. - I do.

2090
01:23:41,880 --> 01:23:43,779
- You're on a dating show. - Yes.

2091
01:23:43,780 --> 01:23:45,480
- You're on a divorce-related show. - Yes.

2092
01:23:45,820 --> 01:23:47,220
- That's impressive. - Whenever...

2093
01:23:47,920 --> 01:23:50,149
I turn the TV on,

2094
01:23:50,150 --> 01:23:51,249
he's always frowning...

2095
01:23:51,250 --> 01:23:52,390
and sighing.

2096
01:23:53,090 --> 01:23:55,359
- This is him. - You can't see him smiling.

2097
01:23:55,360 --> 01:23:57,289
- He's like, "Sir." - Totally.

2098
01:23:57,290 --> 01:23:58,790
And then, he sets it up.

2099
01:23:58,830 --> 01:24:00,760
"Say, for example..."

2100
01:24:01,400 --> 01:24:03,199
Don't you get stressed out at home?

2101
01:24:03,200 --> 01:24:07,470
- Many do worry about me. - Right.

2102
01:24:07,570 --> 01:24:09,609
"Is he mentally okay..."

2103
01:24:09,610 --> 01:24:12,270
"after hearing all those stories?"

2104
01:24:13,010 --> 01:24:14,940
But my...

2105
01:24:16,710 --> 01:24:20,679
I want to show how sincere I am about the guests.

2106
01:24:20,680 --> 01:24:22,920
I'm nothing but genuine in those moments.

2107
01:24:23,490 --> 01:24:25,220
They're like...

2108
01:24:25,860 --> 01:24:27,359
my younger sister and brother,

2109
01:24:27,360 --> 01:24:28,660
older brother,

2110
01:24:29,230 --> 01:24:30,859
and older sister.

2111
01:24:30,860 --> 01:24:33,199
I give them sincere advice,

2112
01:24:33,200 --> 01:24:34,830
hoping they'll live happily.

2113
01:24:35,130 --> 01:24:36,270
But...

2114
01:24:37,670 --> 01:24:38,870
After the show...

2115
01:24:39,840 --> 01:24:40,840
On my way home...

2116
01:24:40,841 --> 01:24:42,299
- Do you get gift vouchers? - No.

2117
01:24:42,300 --> 01:24:43,670
(Cutting in)

2118
01:24:44,170 --> 01:24:46,380
(Financial therapy)

2119
01:24:46,640 --> 01:24:48,709
- I... - That's not impossible.

2120
01:24:48,710 --> 01:24:50,149
I forget about it...

2121
01:24:50,150 --> 01:24:51,750
on my way home after the show.

2122
01:24:52,280 --> 01:24:53,419
You do?

2123
01:24:53,420 --> 01:24:55,120
Yes, because I have more shows tomorrow.

2124
01:24:56,120 --> 01:24:57,490
If I don't forget about it,

2125
01:24:57,790 --> 01:25:00,789
it might affect...

2126
01:25:00,790 --> 01:25:01,919
(Forgetting about it quickly won't get in the way of other shows.)

2127
01:25:01,920 --> 01:25:02,929
the next show.

2128
01:25:02,930 --> 01:25:04,560
That's the mindset I have.

2129
01:25:05,390 --> 01:25:07,200
I shake it off quickly...

2130
01:25:07,430 --> 01:25:09,230
and prepare for the next show.

2131
01:25:11,770 --> 01:25:13,370
Earlier, I monitored...

2132
01:25:13,500 --> 01:25:16,709
- the show from start to finish. - I see.

2133
01:25:16,710 --> 01:25:17,869
The last question was,

2134
01:25:17,870 --> 01:25:21,209
"What does it mean to be truly rich?"

2135
01:25:21,210 --> 01:25:23,080
I heard the question was from you, Jang Hoon.

2136
01:25:23,280 --> 01:25:24,350
Correct.

2137
01:25:24,610 --> 01:25:25,920
What's the answer?

2138
01:25:26,420 --> 01:25:29,119
Who do you think is truly rich?

2139
01:25:29,120 --> 01:25:30,189
Like, what kind of a person.

2140
01:25:30,190 --> 01:25:31,689
(Who does My Star think is truly rich?)

2141
01:25:31,690 --> 01:25:32,790
For me,

2142
01:25:33,420 --> 01:25:36,490
it keeps changing as I grow old.

2143
01:25:37,090 --> 01:25:40,760
- Right now, at my age, - You're right.

2144
01:25:42,600 --> 01:25:43,800
someone who is truly rich...

2145
01:25:45,000 --> 01:25:46,500
has a big heart.

2146
01:25:47,700 --> 01:25:49,509
Someone with a big heart.

2147
01:25:49,510 --> 01:25:50,640
(My forehead is big.)

2148
01:25:50,970 --> 01:25:53,310
And someone easygoing. That's who is truly rich.

2149
01:25:53,710 --> 01:25:55,910
If someone is wealthy...

2150
01:25:56,050 --> 01:25:57,950
but narrow-minded?

2151
01:25:58,810 --> 01:26:00,580
From what I can see,

2152
01:26:01,380 --> 01:26:02,620
- they may... - Yes?

2153
01:26:02,690 --> 01:26:04,020
not become...

2154
01:26:04,150 --> 01:26:07,560
truly rich in the near future.

2155
01:26:08,720 --> 01:26:10,159
Someone with a big heart.

2156
01:26:10,160 --> 01:26:11,960
- That's a tough one. - Yes.

2157
01:26:12,230 --> 01:26:14,329
Who I think is a billionaire is...

2158
01:26:14,330 --> 01:26:15,500
- Yes? - Who is it?

2159
01:26:15,660 --> 01:26:17,400
someone who spends money freely on me.

2160
01:26:18,030 --> 01:26:19,070
What?

2161
01:26:19,130 --> 01:26:20,769
Someone who spends freely on me...

2162
01:26:20,770 --> 01:26:22,570
- A billionaire? - is a true billionaire.

2163
01:26:22,840 --> 01:26:24,170
Really?

2164
01:26:24,910 --> 01:26:26,139
Such a person...

2165
01:26:26,140 --> 01:26:28,010
won't be generous only with me.

2166
01:26:28,240 --> 01:26:30,350
They're someone who knows how to be generous to others.

2167
01:26:30,480 --> 01:26:31,780
Someone who spends a lot.

2168
01:26:32,780 --> 01:26:35,220
Those who spend freely on me are the truly rich.

2169
01:26:36,790 --> 01:26:38,419
Someone with a big heart...

2170
01:26:38,420 --> 01:26:40,259
who knows how to show kindness.

2171
01:26:40,260 --> 01:26:41,459
(Someone who shows kindness with their big heart)

2172
01:26:41,460 --> 01:26:44,090
Kwang Kyu, what kind of a person do you think is truly rich?

2173
01:26:44,160 --> 01:26:45,229
Seo Jang Hoon.

2174
01:26:45,230 --> 01:26:46,899
(An immediate answer)

2175
01:26:46,900 --> 01:26:48,500
That's a clear answer.

2176
01:26:51,270 --> 01:26:52,399
I love it.

2177
01:26:52,400 --> 01:26:54,569
(I love it.)

2178
01:26:54,570 --> 01:26:56,239
I had too much...

2179
01:26:56,240 --> 01:26:58,269
of a prejudice about Jang Hoon.

2180
01:26:58,270 --> 01:27:00,240
That fussiness you see on variety shows.

2181
01:27:00,610 --> 01:27:01,979
Complaining all the time.

2182
01:27:01,980 --> 01:27:04,250
Cussing and getting angry.

2183
01:27:04,350 --> 01:27:06,119
My assumptions about his expressions...

2184
01:27:06,120 --> 01:27:08,350
were shattered into a million pieces today.

2185
01:27:08,650 --> 01:27:11,389
Hanging out with him outside...

2186
01:27:11,390 --> 01:27:14,390
made me realize his childlike innocence.

2187
01:27:14,490 --> 01:27:16,159
Jang Hoon is an open-minded guy...

2188
01:27:16,160 --> 01:27:17,360
with a soft heart.

2189
01:27:17,960 --> 01:27:19,359
- In simple words. - Really,

2190
01:27:19,360 --> 01:27:20,999
today...

2191
01:27:21,000 --> 01:27:22,500
(How was it being taken care of today?)

2192
01:27:22,600 --> 01:27:24,199
Had it not been for the two guys,

2193
01:27:24,200 --> 01:27:25,570
the show...

2194
01:27:25,830 --> 01:27:28,500
might have been...

2195
01:27:29,510 --> 01:27:31,510
a little lonely midway.

2196
01:27:32,640 --> 01:27:35,410
But because the two guys I adore...

2197
01:27:35,640 --> 01:27:37,050
came...

2198
01:27:38,210 --> 01:27:41,280
all the way to Gangneung with me,

2199
01:27:41,720 --> 01:27:43,090
chatted...

2200
01:27:43,890 --> 01:27:45,489
with me,

2201
01:27:45,490 --> 01:27:46,759
and hung around with me,

2202
01:27:46,760 --> 01:27:49,290
I had a lot of fun.

2203
01:27:49,360 --> 01:27:50,730
I really appreciate it too.

2204
01:27:51,090 --> 01:27:52,590
If there's another chance,

2205
01:27:52,960 --> 01:27:55,300
I'd love to...

2206
01:27:55,530 --> 01:27:57,870
take care of those two.

2207
01:27:58,200 --> 01:27:59,670
I'm serious.

2208
01:28:00,300 --> 01:28:03,110
Anyway, that's how grateful I am.

2209
01:28:03,510 --> 01:28:05,140
- A warm thinker. - A warm thinker.

2210
01:28:05,170 --> 01:28:06,279
- Nice one. - Right?

2211
01:28:06,280 --> 01:28:08,779
(My Star is the warmest thinker.)

2212
01:28:08,780 --> 01:28:10,250
A warm-hearted thinker.

2213
01:28:11,244 --> 01:28:12,473
Do we welcome them?

2214
01:28:12,474 --> 01:28:13,644
Why is it different from the usual?

2215
01:28:13,974 --> 01:28:15,243
(My Stars CHOONGJU JI-C)

2216
01:28:15,244 --> 01:28:16,414
(Ji Ye Eun and Jee Seok Jin)

2217
01:28:16,544 --> 01:28:18,183
(The surprise guest CHOONGJU JI-C...)

2218
01:28:18,184 --> 01:28:20,083
(is at Chungju Music Festival!)

2219
01:28:20,084 --> 01:28:22,414
Are you rehearsing at K Karaoke?

2220
01:28:22,984 --> 01:28:24,483
(Raw live vocals hanging by a thread)

2221
01:28:24,484 --> 01:28:26,293
You're not good enough to stand on stage.

2222
01:28:26,294 --> 01:28:28,254
Even your moves aren't in sync.

2223
01:28:28,454 --> 01:28:31,394
(Outraged by the secretaries' brutal honesty)

2224
01:28:31,564 --> 01:28:34,194
(Even at the surprise CHOONGJU JI-C fan sign meeting)

2225
01:28:34,434 --> 01:28:35,563
(I want Lee Seo Jin's autograph.)

2226
01:28:35,564 --> 01:28:36,603
(Not ours?)

2227
01:28:36,604 --> 01:28:37,934
- You want Lee Seo Jin's? - Yes.

2228
01:28:38,134 --> 01:28:39,404
(I also want Lee Seo Jin's autograph.)

2229
01:28:39,574 --> 01:28:40,704
It's them today.

2230
01:28:40,904 --> 01:28:44,144
(The fans leave the fan sign meeting.)

2231
01:28:44,304 --> 01:28:46,074
(More complaints over the fan rivalry)

2232
01:28:46,144 --> 01:28:48,044
(Did you finally speak your mind?)

2233
01:28:48,174 --> 01:28:49,544
(No, he's scary.)

2234
01:28:49,644 --> 01:28:51,414
(My Star even pretended to be asleep.)

2235
01:28:51,544 --> 01:28:52,643
Seo Jin...

2236
01:28:52,644 --> 01:28:54,654
still wants to be the center of attention.

2237
01:28:54,814 --> 01:28:58,383
(My Star talks up a storm behind his back.)

2238
01:28:58,384 --> 01:28:59,824
(Just before the big performance)

2239
01:28:59,924 --> 01:29:01,154
People are packing up.

2240
01:29:01,194 --> 01:29:02,794
They don't know it's our turn.

2241
01:29:02,924 --> 01:29:05,263
(An unprecedented audience walkout?)

2242
01:29:05,264 --> 01:29:06,393
Please stop them.

2243
01:29:06,394 --> 01:29:07,563
Everyone left.

2244
01:29:07,564 --> 01:29:12,564
(Can My Stars finish the performance without a hitch?)

2245
01:29:13,034 --> 01:29:15,674
(My Genie Secretary)
